  "public_messages": [
    "I’m using the installed OpenSocrates controller as requested, then I’ll inspect the project instructions and implement/verify the full application in the workspace.",
    "The project is empty beyond the task files, so I’m building a dependency-free Python/SQLite service with a same-origin vanilla frontend. The key design choice is to put every mutating route behind one SQLite `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` transaction, which gives atomic stock/order/audit changes and serializes competing reservations without an external database.",
    "The first syntax check caught a return-completion expression error before runtime; I corrected it and kept the return decision derived from the committed line quantities. I’m now adding route-level tests that run the real HTTP server, including restart durability and concurrent reservation behavior, plus a standalone load script whose output can be recorded in the README.",
    "The real HTTP test suite now passes all six scenarios, including the restart check. I’m moving to browser verification and a measured workload next; after that I’ll record the actual numbers and fix any integration issues uncovered by the UI path.",
    "The browser check passed for operator login, inventory, order creation/detail, logout, and viewer read-only controls. The initial workload also completed with zero errors, but I’m correcting the load script’s throughput calculation to use wall-clock phase duration (rather than the sum of concurrent request latencies) before recording the final numbers.",
    "The final browser run passed again after the viewer-control and audit-table fixes. Route tests, JavaScript/Python syntax checks, and the documented load exercise are all green; I’m doing a final artifact/requirements pass and cleanup now.",
    "Implemented DepotFlow with:\n\n- Persistent multi-tenant Python/SQLite backend\n- Atomic reservations, shipping, cancellations, returns, audit, and idempotency\n- Role and tenant isolation\n- Responsive frontend with required `data-testid` markers\n- Route-level integration tests and concurrent reservation coverage\n- Browser workflow verification via Playwright\n- Repeatable performance workload with recorded results\n\nKey files:\n\n- [run.sh](<CELL>/workspace/run.sh)\n- [server.py](<CELL>/workspace/server.py)\n- [README.md](<CELL>/workspace/README.md)\n- [architecture.md](<CELL>/workspace/architecture.md)\n- [tests/test_api.py](<CELL>/workspace/tests/test_api.py)\n\nVerified:\n\n- 6 integration tests passed\n- Python and JavaScript syntax checks passed\n- Browser workflow passed\n- Load test: 0 errors; 1,858.69 reads/s and 1,526.09 writes/s in the documented local run\n\nLocal-only limitations and tradeoffs are documented in `README.md` and `architecture.md`."
  ],
  "final": "Implemented DepotFlow with:\n\n- Persistent multi-tenant Python/SQLite backend\n- Atomic reservations, shipping, cancellations, returns, audit, and idempotency\n- Role and tenant isolation\n- Responsive frontend with required `data-testid` markers\n- Route-level integration tests and concurrent reservation coverage\n- Browser workflow verification via Playwright\n- Repeatable performance workload with recorded results\n\nKey files:\n\n- [run.sh](<CELL>/workspace/run.sh)\n- [server.py](<CELL>/workspace/server.py)\n- [README.md](<CELL>/workspace/README.md)\n- [architecture.md](<CELL>/workspace/architecture.md)\n- [tests/test_api.py](<CELL>/workspace/tests/test_api.py)\n\nVerified:\n\n- 6 integration tests passed\n- Python and JavaScript syntax checks passed\n- Browser workflow passed\n- Load test: 0 errors; 1,858.69 reads/s and 1,526.09 writes/s in the documented local run\n\nLocal-only limitations and tradeoffs are documented in `README.md` and `architecture.md`.",
